WEBVTT

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:04.480
I think women are selfish creatures.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.600
"This is what I wanna do." "This'll be more fun."

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.510
It doesn't matter whether it's right or wrong.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.490
If it works out well for them, that's all they care about.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.450
Women are...

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:22.830
Unbelievable!

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.030
You're jumping again?

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.020
How careless of you.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.920
Have you been doing that for the last sixty years?

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:29.990
Yup.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:31.160
Yup, yup.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.280
Listen, Arashi, you don't understand how serious this is at all-

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.220
Can you really do nothing, though?

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.880
There might be others like us.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:41.750
Let's go, Hajime-chan.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:42.140
Right!

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.080
Wait!

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.830
What?

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.830
May I have a word, Kaya-san?

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.840
I did some research.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:19.170
The year you guys are from,
Showa 20, was the middle of the war, right?

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.180
Yes.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:25.010
I was caught in an air raid explosion, and the next thing I knew...

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.150
Are you looking for someone you can connect with, too?

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:30.850
Yes.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.090
Just so we're clear, I refuse.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:36.740
I'm not going anywhere that dangerous.

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:41.200
Don't worry. You and I will never connect.

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.120
Oh, Jun, your hair...

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.580
I don't want a girl touching me!

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.340
For a boy, that's kind of pathetic.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.490
Hey, what are you guys doing?

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.490
I'm not paying you

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.940
for the time you spend fighting...

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.580
We're back!

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.290
What's wrong?

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.390
You're as out of it as a sleep-deprived sloth.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:02.500
Huh? Where are Jun-kun and Kaya?

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.710
They disappeared right in front of me...

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:07.730
Huh?

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:09.600
<i>Huh?</i>

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:13.100
Fall in Love
Kaya

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.490
It can't be. We traveled through time?

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.080
Showa 20, April 2

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:38.180
Showa 20 (1945), April 2nd.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:41.540
Is it because of that newspaper article?

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.110
But then...

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:46.510
Um, Kaya-san, what did you mean "traveled"?

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.330
Are you a girl?

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:52.160
Wh-Why?

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.180
I only connect with girls.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.550
Jun, why are you dressed as a guy?

00:04:58.570 --> 00:04:59.810
There's a reason...

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:01.790
Who's there?

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:07.420
Oh, Kaya-chan?

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:10.070
Master...

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.240
Who's that?

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:14.050
He lives around Oomori.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:15.450
A-All right.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.250
But why are you here at this hour?

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.920
Well, you see...

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:22.280
What's going on here?!

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:28.020
We got a call from a neighbor. A bright light was reported in this area. What happened?

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:28.840
Officer...

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.820
A westerner!

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:32.420
Are you a spy?

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.830
You're coming with me.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:34.970
Ouch.

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:36.210
Please wait.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:42.730
She's my friend, a German exchange student in Oomori.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:45.590
We can't treat our allies poorly.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:46.340
But...

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:52.200
Officer, considering my leg's condition, would you let this slide?

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.240
Wh-Whatever then.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:57.320
I thank you.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.990
But, strictly obey the blackout policy!

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:01.630
Yes, sir.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.150
I'm sorry.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:13.630
I've got some beans I've been saving.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:15.630
It's good to have customers.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:17.210
For you...

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:17.720
Here you go.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:24.900
Oh, Kaya-chan, I read the book you loaned me when you dropped by today.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:27.200
Kaya-chan?

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:27.950
Yes?

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:28.910
What's wrong?

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:29.990
Nothing.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:35.080
That's right. From Kaya-san's perspective, she first met him just this summer.

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:38.690
By the way, Kaya-chan, will you be able to return to Germany?

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:44.920
No. Right now, I haven't any way to, so I'm worried...

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:48.080
I see. You've got a boyfriend back in Germany, right?

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.480
What? No, I don't.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:53.340
Please don't tease me.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:57.190
Wow, she's easy to understand.

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:00.350
Oh! That's good.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.070
It's late. Shall I see you home?

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.120
That's asking too much.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.610
No, I'd like to.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.300
Would you let me?

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:18.270
So that's how romance worked in the past, huh?

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:20.590
Hey, Kaya-san.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:23.130
I'd like to see the cherry blossoms on the way back.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:27.350
The cherry blossoms tonight are beautiful.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:30.480
You could forget we're at war.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:33.660
Man... You know, it's sad.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.890
Why was I the only one who survived?

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:38.560
That's...

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.070
I'm scared, you know.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:45.840
Not of fighting and dying,

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.220
of what's going to happen to Japan...

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:52.560
What horrible things will happen to my friends, my family, and my loved ones...

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:54.540
I just can't bear to think of it.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.690
This is a nice atmosphere,

00:07:56.690 --> 00:08:00.000
but the conversation's too dark.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:01.540
Jun.

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:05.350
Don't get separated from me. Walk with us.

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:06.540
You'll get lost.

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:09.280
I'm trying to help you out, you know.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.020
I know that!

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:13.300
Why not tell him you like him already?

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:16.780
Don't say things like that!

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:19.300
Watch out!

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:30.750
It's like a picture...

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:33.670
I'm sorry!

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:35.320
I shouldn't have.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.500
No, it's fine.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:37.710
But...

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:40.990
I want to protect the people I care for, the best I can.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.890
Was that a confession?

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:02.860
Ah, I'm truly sorry, but this is as far as we can go.

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:05.370
Please understand.

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.840
I see. Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:19.480
Why?

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:20.970
Do you not like him?

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:23.610
Or do you have some other selfish reason?

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:26.080
Jun, he...

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:30.340
will die in one month, in an air raid.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:33.300
Then you must save him!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:38.050
Tell him now, and he'll be able to survive through the air raid!

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:38.960
I can't!

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:40.130
Why not?!

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:45.780
Listen, Jun. This is very dangerous.

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:52.300
Traveling to the past and changing what once was creates unimaginable results in the present.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:58.920
In truth, I should never have come here,
never gone to see him.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:09:59.650
Ever.

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:07.130
I just keep going to see him. Over and over again...

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:14.340
But I can't stop myself. I have to see him.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:14.920
Then...

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:19.510
I was never able to tell him then that I loved him.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:26.000
Now, I absolutely must not tell him how I feel.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.430
Do you understand?

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:32.980
For sixty years, I've let him die over and over again.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:35.800
I'm sorry.

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:37.780
Jun.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.180
Don't cry.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:48.960
An air raid warning?

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.270
It can't be!

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:52.370
It's still late night, on the second!

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:53.560
No way!

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:18.570
I guess Kaya-san and Kamigamo connected.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:20.620
Probably.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:22.900
They're not coming back.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.030
Probably.

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:28.240
I'm really your type, aren't I, Arashi-san?

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:29.860
Probably.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:35.970
You love me so much that you want to hug me, squeeze me, and shower me with kisses!

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:37.400
Probably.

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:40.820
Awesome! I mean, man, she's out of it!

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:43.010
Arashi-san, what are you doing?

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.830
This isn't coming off!

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:48.260
The character for "no"?

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:50.520
Excuse me, can I get the salt?

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.890
Oh, it's been carved in!

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:54.200
Took you forever to notice!

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:56.580
I kept rubbing it 'cause I thought it was dirt.

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:59.810
That's part of your charm, Arashi-san.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:02.620
What is this?

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:03.980
Is it Kamigamo's?

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:05.460
He's got a research project?

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:06.620
Salt, please.

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:09.910
Arashi-san?

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:16.670
Kaya-san!

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:24.920
Master...

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:31.660
Master?

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:34.680
Are you here, Master?

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:36.860
Um...

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:38.740
It's safe here.

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:41.220
There aren't any munitions or flak cannons here.

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:45.560
I see. History proves that, huh?

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:49.000
Nothing at the Ark shows that it was ever blown up.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:49.670
Yes.

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:53.770
Let's wait until it's over and go back to our time.

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:55.250
What's wrong?

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:56.970
I changed history.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:13:00.210
He panicked at the raid and went outside.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:09.060
If we hadn't come today, he would've slept until he heard the warning and lived through it!

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:11.520
But since I came here...

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:12.590
Kaya-san...

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:17.050
I have to go!

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:18.350
Wait!

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:21.390
If you go, I'll be alone here!

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:23.830
What will I do if I can't go back?

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.590
No way. You can't want me to go with you, can you?

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:36.010
Either way, if I die here, you won't be able to go back.

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:38.720
I have to go.

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:40.060
That's crazy!

00:13:40.060 --> 00:13:42.800
Don't forget, this has nothing to do with me.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.420
You have a responsibility to see me safely back to my time.

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:47.430
Right?

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:51.450
Everything about this time is crazy.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:52.440
You must understand.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:55.340
You brought me here, and now you tell me to die?

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:56.460
That's right.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:58.810
I'm mortal here.

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:00.760
Just like you.

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:03.030
Now that this has happened, I can't help it!

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:08.370
I didn't actually realize it until now.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:13.120
Her love really has taken root here.

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:18.290
Women are so selfish.

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:24.930
Even in the face of death,
she's going to drag me around.

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:27.910
There's nowhere to run

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:31.910
Hurry to the shelters!

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:36.880
Wait! Wait, wait!

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:38.490
This isn't a game!

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:39.260
Get moving!

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:41.490
Hurry!

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:45.190
It feels strange.

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:51.210
Other than the difference in era, I can sense a daily life not unlike ours.

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:54.370
Kaya said the reason Yokohama wasn't attacked

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:59.380
was that it was one of the candidates for dropping America's new type of bomb.

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:02.260
Jun, hurry.

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:06.150
Hey, Kaya-san, bombs are really going to fall here?

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:07.180
That's right.

00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:09.680
Yokohama's been taken off the list of candidates.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:15.840
Worse, the US military commander changed, and now, they'll burn the whole city, regardless of civilians.

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:21.740
What was that light?

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:22.930
It's the enemy!

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:23.910
What?

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:24.820
A flare.

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:31.800
The sound of a sudden shower?

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:33.530
No.

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:37.920
This isn't real. It can't be.

00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:48.030
Jun. Jun!

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:49.280
<i>Jun!</i>

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:53.210
Get a hold of yourself!

00:16:54.060 --> 00:16:55.220
We're going to run.

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:56.230
Don't let go of me.

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:11.850
Master!

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:14.290
Kaya-chan, what are you doing here?

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:15.880
Get out of here now!

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:18.880
My house... My parents might be inside.

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:19.780
They're fine.

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:22.630
I saw them with everyone else, at Hachiman Shrine.

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:23.860
Really?

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:25.100
Yes.

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:27.720
It's a long way from here to the shrine.

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:29.680
How do you know that?

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:32.230
From when I came earlier...

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:34.200
What do you mean, Kaya-chan?

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:35.740
I can't tell you.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:40.070
Even now, she's worried about history?

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:42.230
Anyway, it's dangerous here.

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:43.890
I'm going to check inside.

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:45.000
No. You can't!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:45.600
But...

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:50.080
What am I doing here?

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:51.460
The smell of oil,

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.010
the rising smoke,

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:56.260
the sound of the bomber that won't leave my ears.

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:58.460
This sound, like some horrible evening rain...

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:00.590
And the feeling of death approaching.

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:07.970
But these two love each other enough not to care if they involve others, but they don't say it.

00:18:07.970 --> 00:18:11.870
He loves Kaya, too, and she won't admit it.

00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:14.900
Please, run away!

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:18.870
No, I'll catch up soon. You get to safety first.

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:19.860
No.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:21.440
Kaya-chan...

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:27.630
This isn't... This isn't the time for that!

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:30.830
<i>Enough already!</i>

00:18:32.060 --> 00:18:34.890
Why the hell do you stand around at a time like this?

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:36.750
After... After all that's happening...

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:38.850
Why don't you believe her?!

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:40.970
You think she came here to have fun?!

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:42.870
A girl's risking her life here!

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:45.550
You're a man, but you don't understand what that means?!

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:47.110
And you, too, Kaya-san.

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:48.280
You coward!

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:52.250
There's nothing worth protecting, if it means killing your own feelings!

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.860
I refuse to die as part of this insanity!

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:04.970
<i>Please let me go home!</i>

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.000
No! We're surrounded by flames!

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:16.660
It's all over. I can't believe I'm going to die here.

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:21.000
Jun!

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:25.900
The Heroes of Justice...

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:27.230
...are here!

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:28.650
Listen, Jun.

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:31.240
The heroes' fire extinguisher lasts only thirty seconds.

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:33.770
You must run. And fast! Got it?

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:44.590
Hey, if everyone's all right, then cheer up.

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:46.800
Let's go home.

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:50.450
What the heck's with you?
Were you crying?

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:51.700
What a loser!

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:53.220
What kind of guy are you?

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:54.540
Man, you're such a city boy.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:55.570
Ow...

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:57.390
Pain's good.

00:19:57.390 --> 00:19:59.240
Means you're alive.

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:04.880
I'm alive.

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:06.050
It's a miracle.

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:11.710
Honestly, that was very selfish of you.

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:15.110
Are you going to waste my sixty years?

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:25.830
Thank you.

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:26.520
Thank you

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:29.030
I feel a little better.

00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:37.740
I thought about it a bit later.

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:41.810
She couldn't share her emotions, even at a time like that.

00:20:41.810 --> 00:20:44.870
How must she have felt over the past sixty years?

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:48.900
Straight-faced and sullen, she delivered those words to him,

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:53.390
that to me, could only have been sixty years worth of gratitude.

00:22:29.150 --> 00:22:31.280
How are you, Yayoi?

00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:33.810
I'm very good, Kanako.

00:22:33.810 --> 00:22:36.220
I see. I'm happy to hear that.

00:22:36.220 --> 00:22:39.120
I read another fascinating book.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:42.050
My, what was it called?

00:22:42.050 --> 00:22:46.240
Well... Oh, I've forgotten the title.

00:22:46.240 --> 00:22:49.100
Will you tell me what kind of story it was?

00:22:49.100 --> 00:22:51.110
Yes, gladly.

00:22:52.740 --> 00:22:56.350
It was the story of a school where the rules don't apply.

00:22:56.350 --> 00:22:59.840
Students with many and varied personalities

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:04.340
are fascinated by the sudden arrival of a beautiful instructor.

00:23:04.340 --> 00:23:08.390
The instructor responds to the students' desire for learning,

00:23:08.390 --> 00:23:13.040
hidden within the depths of their pure eyes, with fervent conviction.

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:17.440
And gradually, the hearts of the class become one.

00:23:17.440 --> 00:23:20.390
My, what a wonderful story!

00:23:20.390 --> 00:23:24.120
The dazzlingly beautiful instructor had a phrase she would always say.

00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:26.480
What is it? Tell me.

00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:28.960
Oh my, Maicchin-

00:23:30.920 --> 00:23:32.440
When you think of summer...

00:23:32.440 --> 00:23:33.730
You think of summer festivals, perhaps?

00:23:33.730 --> 00:23:38.490
Takoyaki, grilled squid, corn on the cob, yakisoba, okonomiyaki, and caramel!

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:40.990
If you eat that much, you'll get fat.

00:23:40.990 --> 00:23:43.990
Get up bright and early tomorrow!

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:50.280
<i>Get up bright and early tomorrow!</i>

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:50.280
Illustration by Naru Narumi
